1. Current State Summary
Tech Stack
Backend: Spring Boot 3.5.10 / Java 21, Hibernate JPA, PostgreSQL, Liquibase migrations, Hibernate Spatial (loaded but unused)
Auth: Spring Security + OAuth2 Resource Server, RBAC with 56 tenant permissions
Multi-tenancy: Schema-per-tenant — each tenant gets its own PostgreSQL schema
Frontend: React 19, TypeScript, React Router 7, Vite, Tailwind + Shadcn/ui, custom i18n (EN/AR), Axios with interceptors
What Exists Today
Database Entities
Entity	Table	Notes
StockMovement	stock_movements	Immutable ledger. Types: RECEIVE, TRANSFER_IN, TRANSFER_OUT, ADJUST, PICK. Has lot_number, expiry_date, reference_id, notes, created_by. No source document link.
OnHandEntry	v_on_hand (view)	Aggregates SUM(qty) grouped by (location_id, product_id) — lot_number NOT in key
WarehouseLayout	warehouse_layouts	Active/inactive, one-active constraint
BlockTemplate	block_templates	Reusable node types with identifier_format, side_config, icon_name
LayoutBlock	layout_blocks	Tree nodes: parent_id, position, side. Leaf = selectable location. No location_kind, no scan_code, no stored full path code.
Product	products	Has track_lot, track_expiry booleans. Soft-delete.
Supplier, ProductSupplier, ProductCategory, UnitOfMeasure	—	Full CRUD, soft-delete
AuditLog	audit_log	JSONB before/after state, all entity mutations
Services / Business Logic
Service	What it does
InventoryLedgerService	receive(), transfer() (atomic pair), adjust(), getOnHand(), getMovements(), product/location lookups. Stock sufficiency validation. Lot/expiry validation per product flags.
WarehouseLayoutService	Layout CRUD, activation, classic preset builder
LayoutBlockService	Full tree management: add, batch-add, copy-subtree, move, reassign-template, delete. Position shifting.
TenantProductManagementService	Full product CRUD with supplier associations
TenantAuditService	Entity change logging
API Endpoints
/{tenantSlug}/inventory — receive, transfer, adjust, on-hand, movements, product/location lookups
/{tenantSlug}/warehouse-layouts — layout CRUD + activate/deactivate
/{tenantSlug}/warehouse-layouts/{id}/blocks — full block tree management
/{tenantSlug}/products, /suppliers, /categories, /units-of-measure, /audit-logs
Frontend
Inventory page (3 tabs): Stock (on-hand table), Operations (receive/transfer/adjust forms), Movements (ledger history)
Warehouse Layout Builder (full-featured: block tree, templates, drag/reorder, batch creation)
Product catalog, suppliers, UOMs, categories — full management
RBAC: roles/permissions editor, user management
Paths constant: src/shared/consts/paths.ts
i18n: 772 keys in messages/en.ts and messages/ar.ts
What Does NOT Exist
No location_kind field on LayoutBlock (STORAGE, STAGING, QUARANTINE, etc.)
No scan_code on LayoutBlock
No stored/computed full location path code
No Receipt document (header + lines + lifecycle)
No Dispatch document (header + lines + lifecycle)
No Count Session
No scan resolver endpoint
No QR/label generation
No source document link on stock_movements (only reference_id for transfer pairs)
No reason codes on movements
v_on_hand view doesn't include lot_number in grouping key — lot stock is invisible at the view level
2. Plan Critique
Feature 1 — Location Identity
Assessment: Valid and foundational — schema gaps must be filled

The current LayoutBlock has no scan_code, no location_kind, and no stored full path code. pathLabel is computed dynamically at query time in the location lookup, not stored.

Specific gaps:

backend/.../warehouse/block/LayoutBlock.java — missing locationKind (enum) and scanCode (unique VARCHAR)
V13__replace_f1_with_block_system.sql — layout_blocks table has no kind/scan columns
The plan is correct that only leaf nodes hold stock — this is already enforced by the listLocationLookups() query that excludes parent blocks
One correction to the plan: "stable full location code" should be distinguished from scan_code. The full path label (e.g., A-01-L1-S2) can be computed and stored on write, but you still need a short unique scan_code separately. Both are needed but they're different columns.

The location_kind enum cleanly handles Feature 2 (Special Locations) without a separate table.

Feature 2 — Special Locations
Assessment: Correct design, fully covered by Feature 1 — not a separate feature

The plan is right: STAGING, QUARANTINE, DAMAGED, DISPATCH are just location_kind values, not a status engine. This is the correct approach given the immutable ledger design.

However, the plan implies these are "system-defined" areas. In practice, they should be manager-designated: a warehouse manager marks a block node as kind=STAGING. There's no need to auto-create them. Merge this into Feature 1's scope.

Risk: The permission model needs a new permission for setting location kinds — or it falls under existing WAREHOUSE_BLOCK_EDIT. Reuse WAREHOUSE_BLOCK_EDIT.

Feature 3 — Simple Lot/Batch Tracking
Assessment: Data fields exist; the aggregation gap is the real problem

Product.trackLot, Product.trackExpiry, StockMovement.lotNumber, StockMovement.expiryDate — all already in the schema.

The critical gap is v_on_hand:


-- Current: lot-tracked stock is invisible as separate lines
SELECT location_id, product_id, SUM(qty) AS qty_on_hand
FROM stock_movements GROUP BY location_id, product_id

-- Needed: lot_number must be in the grouping key
SELECT location_id, product_id, lot_number, SUM(qty) AS qty_on_hand
FROM stock_movements GROUP BY location_id, product_id, lot_number
This is a breaking change — every query hitting OnHandEntry/v_on_hand will now return more rows, and the OnHandEntry projection interface needs lotNumber added. The getOnHand() service method and the frontend on-hand display all change.

No Lot table needed for Phase 1. Distinct lots can be queried from stock_movements. Don't build a Lot entity — it's premature.

Feature 4 — Receipts
Assessment: Valid, does not exist, significant addition

The existing POST /inventory/receive creates one RECEIVE movement per call — no document header, no multi-line batch, no lifecycle. It will still be useful for ad-hoc receives but is not a receipt document.

The plan is correct: DRAFT → POSTED → VOID, posting creates RECEIVE movements. Key design point — when posting, the stock_movements.source_document_id (from Feature 11) must be set to the receipt ID for traceability.

Conflict: The existing ad-hoc receive endpoint should remain for now. Receipts are an additive layer on top.

Feature 5 — Putaway
Assessment: No backend needed — the plan is correct

Transfer (POST /inventory/transfer) already works. Putaway is purely a UI workflow: after posting a receipt to STAGING, a worker picks items and calls transfer to the final bin. No new backend module needed.

Recommendation: Drop this as a numbered feature. It's a UI pattern, not a feature chunk.

Feature 6 — Dispatches
Assessment: Valid, symmetric with Receipts, does not exist

The PICK movement type exists in the ledger. No DispatchDocument exists. Same design pattern as receipts — needs header, lines, DRAFT → POSTED → VOID lifecycle.

Stock sufficiency validation (which already exists in InventoryLedgerService.transfer()) must be repeated at dispatch post time. Since lot tracking changes the stock key (Feature 3), dispatch picking by lot must check stock per (location, product, lot).

Feature 7 — Count Sessions
Assessment: Valid, does not exist, depends on lot-level on-hand

The ADJUST movement type exists. A count session needs to snapshot expected stock (from v_on_hand at session-open time) and compare against physically counted quantities. Posting creates ADJUST movements only for variances.

Dependency: Must come after the v_on_hand lot grouping fix (Feature 3) — otherwise, expected quantities for lot-tracked items will be wrong.

Feature 8 — QR/Barcode Labels
Assessment: Backend part is covered by Feature 1; frontend is pure UI work

Once scan_code is on LayoutBlock and products have SKUs, label printing is a frontend concern (generate QR SVG client-side, print-friendly layout). No new backend endpoints needed.

The scan_code for a product can be its SKU. The scan_code for a location comes from Feature 1. Lots can encode as {productSku}:{lotNumber}.

Recommendation: Collapse into Feature 1 (backend scan_code) + a small frontend label component. Not a standalone chunk.

Feature 9 — Scan Workflow
Assessment: Valid, needs one new backend endpoint + frontend components

A unified scan resolver is needed:


GET /{tenantSlug}/scan/resolve?code=XYZ
→ { type: "PRODUCT" | "LOCATION" | "LOT", id: "...", ... }
This endpoint checks:

Is XYZ a product SKU?
Is XYZ a location scan_code?
Is XYZ a lot pattern ({sku}:{lot})?
This is small backend work but has a large frontend payoff — scan input auto-fills forms everywhere.

Feature 10 — Minimal Operational Reporting
Assessment: Partial exists, rest depends on upstream features

Already working:

Stock by location: GET /inventory/on-hand ✓
Movement history: GET /inventory/movements ✓
Missing (and dependent on upstream):

Stock by lot (needs v_on_hand fix from Feature 3)
Stock in operational areas filtered by location_kind (needs Feature 1)
Receipt/dispatch history (needs Features 4/6)
Count variance summary (needs Feature 7)
Recommendation: Don't build a separate reporting module. Add query params to existing endpoints (filter by location_kind, add lot to on-hand response). Build this incrementally alongside each upstream feature.

Feature 11 — Operational Traceability
Assessment: Valid, needs schema addition — do it early

Currently stock_movements has only reference_id (used for transfer pairs). There is no link from a RECEIVE movement to its receipt document, or from a PICK to its dispatch.

Needs two new columns on stock_movements:

source_document_id UUID — links to receipt_id, dispatch_id, or count_session_id
reason_code VARCHAR(50) — optional reason for adjustments
These columns should be added before Receipt and Dispatch documents are built, otherwise you'll need a second migration later.

3. Implementation Roadmap
Listed in dependency order. Each chunk is independently testable.

Chunk 1 — Location Kind + Scan Code (Medium)
Scope: Add location_kind and scan_code to LayoutBlock. Add auto-generated full_code (stored path label like A-01-L1-S2).

Files affected:

backend/.../warehouse/block/LayoutBlock.java — add 3 new fields
backend/.../warehouse/block/LayoutBlockService.java — generate scan_code on insert/copy, validate uniqueness, allow setting location_kind
backend/.../warehouse/block/LayoutBlockController.java — add kind to update metadata request
backend/resources/db/migration/tenant/V18__add_location_identity.sql — add columns, unique index on scan_code
frontend/.../types/warehouse.ts — add locationKind, scanCode, fullCode to WarehouseBlockResult
frontend/.../warehouse/WarehouseLayoutsPage.tsx — show kind badge, allow kind selection on leaf nodes
frontend/src/i18n/messages/en.ts + ar.ts — kind labels
Dependencies: None — this is the foundation.

Migration risk: Additive only. Existing rows get location_kind = STORAGE by default, scan_code auto-generated from current path. Nullable initially.

GIS relevance: Critical — the GIS layer will reference locations by scan_code and color-code by location_kind.

Chunk 2 — Lot-Level On-Hand View (Small, but breaking)
Scope: Add lot_number to the v_on_hand grouping key. Update all downstream types and queries.

Files affected:

V19__update_v_on_hand_lot_grouping.sql — DROP VIEW v_on_hand; CREATE VIEW v_on_hand AS ... GROUP BY location_id, product_id, lot_number
backend/.../inventory/OnHandEntry.java — add lotNumber to projection
backend/.../inventory/StockMovementRepository.java — update native queries for on-hand
backend/.../inventory/InventoryLedgerService.java — update getOnHand() result mapping, update stock sufficiency check (must now match lot when lot is required)
frontend/.../types/inventory.ts — add lotNumber to OnHandEntry
frontend/.../inventory/InventoryPage.tsx — show lot column in stock tab when applicable
Dependencies: None, but do this before Receipts/Dispatches/Count Sessions.

Migration risk: Breaking — the view returns more rows for lot-tracked products. Frontend on-hand table changes. Test the transfer sufficiency check — it must now sum stock at (location, product, lot) for lot-tracked products.

Chunk 3 — Stock Movement Traceability Fields (Small)
Scope: Add source_document_id and reason_code to stock_movements. Update the entity and service to accept/pass these fields.

Files affected:

V20__add_movement_traceability.sql — add nullable source_document_id UUID, reason_code VARCHAR(50) to stock_movements
backend/.../inventory/StockMovement.java — add fields
backend/.../inventory/InventoryLedgerService.java — update all operation methods to accept optional sourceDocumentId and reasonCode
backend/.../inventory/InventoryLedgerController.java — update AdjustRequest to accept optional reasonCode
frontend/.../types/inventory.ts — add sourceDocumentId, reasonCode to MovementResult
frontend/.../inventory/InventoryPage.tsx — show reason code in movements tab; add optional reason field to adjust form
Dependencies: None. Do before Receipts/Dispatches.

Migration risk: Additive only (nullable columns). No existing behavior changes.

Chunk 4 — Receipt Documents (Large)
Scope: Multi-line inbound document with header, lines, DRAFT → POSTED → VOID lifecycle. Posting calls InventoryLedgerService.receive() for each line and stamps source_document_id.

Files affected:

Backend (new files):

