Chunk 6 — Count Sessions (Large)
Scope: Controlled stocktaking. Open session for selected locations, capture physical counts, post variances as ADJUST movements.

Files affected:

Backend (new files):

tenant/counting/CountSession.java — id, name, status (OPEN/COUNTING/POSTED/VOID), location_ids (JSON array or junction table), opened_at, posted_at
tenant/counting/CountLine.java — id, session_id, location_id, product_id, lot_number (nullable), expected_qty (snapshotted at open), counted_qty (entered by user), variance
tenant/counting/CountSessionService.java:
openSession(locationIds, name) — creates session, snapshots v_on_hand for selected locations into CountLines as expected_qty
updateCount(sessionId, lineId, countedQty) — enters physical count
postSession(sessionId) — for each line where variance ≠ 0: call adjust(variance, sourceDocumentId=sessionId, reasonCode=COUNT_ADJUSTMENT)
voidSession(sessionId) — only if not POSTED
tenant/counting/CountSessionController.java — /{tenantSlug}/count-sessions
V23__create_count_sessions.sql
Frontend (new files):

features/tenant/counting/ directory
CountSessionsPage.tsx, api/countingApi.ts, types/counting.ts
Frontend (modified):

routes.tsx, TenantNavbar.tsx, paths.ts, i18n files
Dependencies: Chunks 2 (lot-level expected stock), 3 (source_document_id on adjustments)

Migration risk: New tables only.

Chunk 7 — Scan Resolver + Label Components (Medium)
Scope: One backend endpoint to resolve a scanned code. Frontend scan input component that auto-fills forms. Print-friendly label templates for locations, products, lots.

Files affected:

Backend (new files):

tenant/scan/ScanController.java — GET /{tenantSlug}/scan/resolve?code=XYZ
tenant/scan/ScanResolverService.java:
Check if code matches a product SKU → return {type: PRODUCT, product: {...}}
Check if code matches a layout_blocks.scan_code → return {type: LOCATION, location: {...}}
Check if code matches {sku}:{lotNumber} pattern and lot exists in movements → return {type: LOT, product: {...}, lotNumber: "..."}
Frontend (new files):

shared/components/ScanInput.tsx — text input with scan icon, fires callback on Enter/paste with resolved entity
features/tenant/labels/LocationLabel.tsx — print-friendly QR label for a location
features/tenant/labels/ProductLabel.tsx — print-friendly QR label for a product
Frontend (modified):

ReceiptsPage.tsx — embed ScanInput in product and location fields
DispatchesPage.tsx — same
CountSessionsPage.tsx — same
InventoryPage.tsx (Operations tab) — add scan input to receive/transfer/adjust forms
Dependencies: Chunk 1 (scan_code on locations), Chunks 4/5/6 (forms to auto-fill)

Migration risk: None. Additive.

