4. GIS Readiness Checklist
These are the conditions that must be true before Phase 2 (GIS) can begin:


Foundations
[ ] Every leaf LayoutBlock has a stable, unique scan_code — Chunk 1
[ ] Every leaf LayoutBlock has a location_kind that GIS can use for color-coding — Chunk 1
[ ] v_on_hand correctly breaks out stock by (location, product, lot) — Chunk 2
[ ] Every stock movement links back to its source document — Chunk 3

Operational Workflows
[ ] Inbound stock enters via Receipt documents (not just raw receives) — Chunk 4
[ ] Outbound stock leaves via Dispatch documents (not just raw picks) — Chunk 5
[ ] Stocktaking is done via Count Sessions with variance posting — Chunk 6
[ ] Stock in operational areas (STAGING, QUARANTINE) is clearly identified by location_kind — Chunk 1

Integration Surface
[ ] Scan resolver endpoint exists: GET /scan/resolve?code=XYZ — Chunk 7
[ ] Location scan_codes are printable (QR labels) so workers can scan physical locations — Chunk 7

GIS Phase Can Start When
[ ] Phase 2 can attach (x, y, z) or polygon geometry to LayoutBlock rows by ID
[ ] Phase 2 can query on-hand stock per location and render it on the map
[ ] Phase 2 can show "what kind" each zone is (STAGING in yellow, QUARANTINE in red, etc.)
[ ] Phase 2 can highlight active receipt/dispatch documents on the map
[ ] Phase 2 can accept a scanned location code and pan the map to it
Build Order Summary
#	Chunk	Complexity	Blocks
1	Location Kind + Scan Code	Medium	Nothing
2	Lot-Level On-Hand View	Small	Nothing (do early)
3	Movement Traceability Fields	Small	Nothing (do early)
4	Receipt Documents	Large	1, 2, 3
5	Dispatch Documents	Large	1, 2, 3
6	Count Sessions	Large	2, 3
7	Scan Resolver + Labels	Medium	1, 4, 5, 6
8	Reporting Gaps	Small	All
Dropped from original plan as separate features: Putaway (UI pattern only, no backend), standalone lot table (unnecessary), standalone reporting module (extend existing endpoints instead), label generation as a module (collapse into Chunk 1 + Chunk 7).







